{"assets":["/editorial-assets/0418ec77afa5c3daac167b1ccfb2c5dc1e3f406bf3f152e4a46f87657f23f030.png","/editorial-assets/19d94dcf385729269a2ea8b674bb040c902d09ad34968d0c441dfb4e0cc34873.png","/editorial-assets/676d135fd1b10c9c330687eeabb8d0b6ffb5584bd325a1f3faeeb534e9654517.png","/editorial-assets/fc12636225d027e5b8b2ced0910153656c9454c56cf9915df1b2b11e0be9c460.png","/editorial-assets/ec0b0b271386a3da4e74664848ecae4449b04575636e78c12f5fd29acb32a420.png","/editorial-assets/7d44990fddadb67d2dfd0c8870787b6416dcac91513a317ad8e753f94348c19b.png","/editorial-assets/f6716cbc55e93bdceef3c820687fe07b8a5aeb068be01c0ddb3e8a00be628c64.png"],"contestId":"937","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"937A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/937/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"937A - Olympiad"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Drop all participants with zero points. Then the answer is simply the number of distinct points among the remaining participants."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prepared by "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/vintage_Vlad_Makeev"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"vintage_Vlad_Makeev"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"937B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/937/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"937B - Vile Grasshoppers"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first observation is that the optimal branch shouldn't be divisible by anything in range [2.."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]. Let us decrease "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" until its minimal divisor (other than one) is greater than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Why does this approach work? Note that the the nearest prime less or equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is valid. At the same time the prime gap of numbers less than billion doesn't exceed 300 and we're gonna factorize no more than 300 numbers in total. Therefore the complexity is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0418ec77afa5c3daac167b1ccfb2c5dc1e3f406bf3f152e4a46f87657f23f030.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prepared by "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/GreenGrape"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"GreenGrape"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"936A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/936/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"936A - Save Energy!"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" There are repeated segments in the cooking process, that are between two consecutive moments, when Julia turns the stove on. Let's call such segment a period. Consider two cases: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", when Julia comes, the stove is always off, that means "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"period"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In other case Julia comes to the kitchen "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" times between two turnings on, when the stove is still on, and does nothing. In this case "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a number such that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the stove is on, ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1)·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the stove is off. Then the period is ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1)·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to ⌈ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"⌉ - 1. So "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"period"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = ⌈ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"⌉·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Let's say the chicken consists of 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" independent parts. On the working stove two parts of the chicken are prepared per minute. If the stove is off, one part is prepared. Let's find the number of prepared parts during one period: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cooking"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"period"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"period"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and we need "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"num"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = ⌊ 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cooking"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"⌋ whole periods. After that we still have "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"carry"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"num"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cooking"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" parts left to cook. "},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"carry"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", chicken will be prepared after "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"carry"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes the stove will be on and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"carry"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" it will be off. Thus the answer is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"num"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"period"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"carry"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Otherwise "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"carry"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" parts become ready after "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"carry"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 2 minutes and answer is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"num"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"period"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"carry"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 2. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prepared by "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/dusja.ds"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dusja.ds"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"936B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/936/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"936B - Sleepy Game"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the answer is sequence of adjacent vertices of even length such that the last vertex of this sequence has no outgoing edges."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Build state graph as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"State is pair ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"parity"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is vertex of initial graph and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"parity"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is parity of count of vertices on path from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". For every edge "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"uv"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of initial graph add edges "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/19d94dcf385729269a2ea8b674bb040c902d09ad34968d0c441dfb4e0cc34873.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/676d135fd1b10c9c330687eeabb8d0b6ffb5584bd325a1f3faeeb534e9654517.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" in state graph. So there exists path from ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", 1) to ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"parity"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") if and only if there exists path from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in initial graph of parity "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"parity"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lets find all reachable from ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", 1) states using BFS or DFS. If there is state ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", 0) among them such that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" has no outgoing edges in initial graph, then Petya can win. He can move along vertices in path from ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", 1) to ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", 0) in state graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise we need to check if Petya can make 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" moves for drawing a tie. If there is a tie then the chip visited some vertex twice, because "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Therefore it is sufficient to check if there is a cycle in initial graph reachable from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". In this case Petya can play as follows: move to any vertex of cycle and then move along the cycle as long as it requires to draw a tie."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prepared by "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/pashka"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pashka"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/YakutovDmitriy"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YakutovDmitriy"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"936C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/936/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"936C - Lock Puzzle"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The answer is «NO» only in the case when multisets of letters in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" differ. In all other cases there is a solution."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's construct the solution uses "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/fc12636225d027e5b8b2ced0910153656c9454c56cf9915df1b2b11e0be9c460.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" operations. To do that, you need to «add» two symbols to current already built substring using five operations. You can do it, for example, using the following method (the underlined string is chosen as β):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"...x...abc "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ec0b0b271386a3da4e74664848ecae4449b04575636e78c12f5fd29acb32a420.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"cba......x "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cba......x "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ec0b0b271386a3da4e74664848ecae4449b04575636e78c12f5fd29acb32a420.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"x......abc "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x......abc "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ec0b0b271386a3da4e74664848ecae4449b04575636e78c12f5fd29acb32a420.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"cbax...... "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cbax...y.. "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ec0b0b271386a3da4e74664848ecae4449b04575636e78c12f5fd29acb32a420.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"..ycbax... "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"..ycbax... "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ec0b0b271386a3da4e74664848ecae4449b04575636e78c12f5fd29acb32a420.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":".....ycbax "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If we had abc as suffix, after these operations, we get ycbax, which is two symbols longer. Choosing x and y accordingly, we can maintain maintain the invariant, that the suffix of current string always contains monotone (increasing or decreasing) sequence. After we make this sequence have length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", the entire string is either a cyclic shift or a reversed cyclic shift of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". You can do cyclic shift by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in three operations: «shift "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"», «shift "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"», «shift "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"». This way, we get a "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/7d44990fddadb67d2dfd0c8870787b6416dcac91513a317ad8e753f94348c19b.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" solution. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prepared by "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/dusja.ds"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dusja.ds"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/VArtem"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"VArtem"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"936D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/936/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"936D - World of Tank"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At first arrange a pair of facts:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If there is a path which doesn't contain blowed cell you can easily convert it to path which does. So it's enough to check such paths to determine answer."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Tank can accumulate shots when it moves without turns. In other words: consider tank makes 100 steps without turns and shots, so lets say that tank accumulate 100 steps. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to 3 tank was able to make 33 shots on that part of path. Accumulating steps is the same as deferred shots. Tank gains steps and when it's necessary to make some shots we can choose position of shots on this straight part of path in such way that tank blows obstacles. But when the tank changes its row you should flush accumulated steps to minimum of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and old value because accumulated steps has sense only on hte straight line without shots because otherwise it may be impossible to choose correct positions for shots."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second step is solution with asymptotics "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Using dynamic programming: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] — maximal number of accumulated step if tank is in cell with coordinates ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and -1 if it's impossible. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You should update dynamic's values from previous cell in the same row or cell in another row but in the same column."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Check that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1] ≠  - 1 (otherwise tank can't be in the ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1) cell) after that update value by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1] + 1 if there is no obstacle in cell ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1] - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Before updating by cell in another row you should update both of them ((1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and (2, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") if rows numerated from 1) by cells in previous column and only after that you can update them be each other."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Store for each cell ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") was it updated from (3 - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") or ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1). Start from last column and iterate to the zero one to restore the path."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When you restore path you can easily calculate number of obstacles which should be blowed for each part of path without shots. So now you have to choose places for them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider any part of the path from any turn to the next one. Let there are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" obstacles, so all of them must be destroyed by the tank. Let the first cell of this path's part has coordinates ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", so the first shot on this part can be not earlier than ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the next one not earlier than ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and so on. Place shots in that position and tank will correctly blow up all obstacles. It obviously follows from dynamic programming's definition. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third step is prooving that tank can turn only to cells which are immediately after an obstacle (if obstacle is in cell with coordinates ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") then tank turns to cell ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1))."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider any path which is one of soloutions. Consider the first turn in this path which doesn't fit the constraint above. Then consider the nearest obstacle in the same row as row where tank will be after turn, but with smaller number of a column."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If tank turns to the cell which immediately after that obstacle then it can move along that row to current position, eliminates unnecessary turns, so the considered turn will be eliminated."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Otherwise tank was in another row, so you can easily turn and do the same actions to eliminate such turn."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Repeat this actions you transform any path to path which has only turns to cells immediately after obstacles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sort obstacles in order of increasing their column's number. So due to fact that tank can turn only in certain points it isn't necessary calculates DP for all 2·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" cells. Now "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" cells enough. So calculate the same DP for cells which are immediatel after obstacles, strore for each point the point where it was updated from to restore path. Restore path and for each part without turns calculate number of obstacles to destroy and place shots."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Complexity "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prepared by "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/dusja.ds"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dusja.ds"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/burakov28"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"burakov28"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"936E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/936/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"936E - Iqea"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's cut the figure into strips of consecutive cells which lie in the same column. Consider strips as vertices. Connect two vertices by an edge if their strips have common edge. It can be proved that resulting graph is a tree. Consider two cells $$$(x_a, y_a)$$$ and $$$(x_b, y_b)$$$. Cell $$$(x_a, y_a)$$$ lies on strip $$$v_a$$$, cell $$$(x_b, y_b)$$$ lies on strip $$$v_b$$$. Then any shortest path between these two cells goes only through strips corresponding to vertices on path from $$$v_a$$$ to $$$v_b$$$. And every such strip has non-empty intersection with path between this two cells. So if we build centroid decomposition of tree of strips, shortest path between two cells will surely go through strip of centroid which divide vertices of these two cells."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, you can solve standard problem on tree: sometimes vertices are turning on, and you are to find the distance to the nearest vertex that is turned on. To solve this problem you can use centroid decomposition. Only one question left. How to combine distances from centroid to two cells? Consider two cells $$$(x_a, y_a)$$$ and $$$(x_b, y_b)$$$, and path between them. Let this path goes through strip $$$v_c$$$. Let $$$d_a$$$ be a distance from $$$(x_a, y_a)$$$ to the strip $$$v_c$$$, $$$z_a$$$ be a $$$y$$$ coordinate of nearest cell on strip $$$v_c$$$. The same way define $$$d_b$$$ and $$$z_b$$$ for cell $$$(x_b, y_b)$$$. Then the distance between $$$(x_a, y_a)$$$ and $$$(x_b, y_b)$$$ equals to $$$d_a + d_b + |z_a - z_b|$$$. So we can store $$$h$$$ values in every vertex and change them in the following way: $$$val_i = \\min(val_i, d_a + |z_i - z_a|)$$$, $$$h$$$ is the size of strip, $$$z_i$$$ is the $$$y$$$ coordinate of $$$i$$$-th cell on strip. This can be done using segment tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example of building a tree. Blue and yellow colors mark cells $$$(x_a, y_a)$$$ and $$$(x_b, y_b)$$$. Green color marks strip $$$v_c$$$. The values are: $$$d_a = 6$$$, $$$d_b = 7$$$, $$$z_a = 8$$$, $$$z_b = 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f6716cbc55e93bdceef3c820687fe07b8a5aeb068be01c0ddb3e8a00be628c64.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"I honestly don't know if this is the picture originally drawn for this tutorial. The original picture in Metapost doesn't compile, and I asked ChatGPT to redraw it for me... "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Values $$$d_a$$$ and $$$z_a$$$ for every pair cell and vertex can be calculated during building of centroid decomposition."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Complexity of the solution is $$$O(n\\cdot log(n) + q\\cdot log^2(n))$$$ time and $$$O(n\\cdot log(n))$$$ memory."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prepared by "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/budalnik"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"budalnik"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/58056"}